1
00:00:02,384 --> 00:00:03,552
CONGRATS ON NATIONALS

2
00:00:03,635 --> 00:00:07,848
[Taiki] <i>Nationals are over,
and we're nearing the end of summer break.</i>

3
00:00:07,931 --> 00:00:10,475
<i>It's time we start worrying
about unfinished homework.</i>

4
00:00:10,559 --> 00:00:11,435
AUGUST 26

5
00:00:11,518 --> 00:00:12,811
{\an8}ASSIGNMENT
OFFENSE/DEFENSE

6
00:00:12,894 --> 00:00:15,939
{\an8}<i>But on this day, August 26th...</i>

7
00:00:16,022 --> 00:00:16,940
[popping]

8
00:00:17,023 --> 00:00:17,899
[exclaims]

9
00:00:17,983 --> 00:00:19,192
[Nagisa] Hey, Chii!

10
00:00:19,276 --> 00:00:21,445
[all] Happy Birthday, Chinatsu!

11
00:00:22,696 --> 00:00:23,697
Thank you so much!

12
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,824
- [laughter]
- All right, here you go.

13
00:00:26,324 --> 00:00:28,201
Let's put this on.

14
00:00:28,285 --> 00:00:29,786
[girl] I have a present for you.

15
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:31,246
[Chinatsu] Ooh, what is it?

16
00:00:31,788 --> 00:00:33,707
DEER

17
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:36,793
[Nagisa] A Chinatsu original deer,
now on a shirt!

18
00:00:36,877 --> 00:00:38,712
- Wear it at practice.
- [gasps]

19
00:00:40,046 --> 00:00:41,840
Say cheese, girls.

20
00:00:41,923 --> 00:00:43,800
[all] Cheese!

21
00:00:43,884 --> 00:00:44,843
[camera shutter clicks]

22
00:00:46,928 --> 00:00:48,930
[opening theme song playing]

23
00:01:13,246 --> 00:01:16,666
BLUE BOX

24
00:02:16,017 --> 00:02:16,852
{\an8}- [laughter]
- Wow!

25
00:02:16,935 --> 00:02:17,936
{\an8}EPISODE 15
AUGUST 26

26
00:02:18,019 --> 00:02:18,895
{\an8}Nice one! Let me see.

27
00:02:18,979 --> 00:02:20,939
{\an8}Girls are into that kind of thing,
aren't they?

28
00:02:21,022 --> 00:02:23,441
- [boy 2] It's a cuteness overload.
- [Nagisa] So funny.

29
00:02:24,151 --> 00:02:25,694
It's her birthday, apparently.

30
00:02:25,777 --> 00:02:26,695
I know that!

31
00:02:27,487 --> 00:02:29,781
I've been gathering information
for weeks now.

32
00:02:29,865 --> 00:02:32,742
Running comparisons of gifts,
making pros and cons.

33
00:02:32,826 --> 00:02:36,079
What if I get her the same thing
as someone else, or do too much?

34
00:02:36,163 --> 00:02:39,583
Picking out a birthday present isn't easy.

35
00:02:40,709 --> 00:02:42,335
And then, well...

36
00:02:42,961 --> 00:02:47,465
ever since nationals,
I feel like she's been a little down.

37
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:52,095
<i>So I kind of figured
she didn't want a big celebration.</i>

38
00:02:52,178 --> 00:02:53,722
- [laughter]
- [Kyo] Mm?

39
00:02:53,805 --> 00:02:54,848
[Nagisa] Let's celebrate!

40
00:02:55,473 --> 00:02:58,602
However! I'll figure
something out by toni-- [grunts]

41
00:02:59,895 --> 00:03:01,104
- [Hina] Oh.
- [Taiki] Huh?

42
00:03:01,187 --> 00:03:02,564
My bad, sorry.

43
00:03:03,732 --> 00:03:05,817
Hina! You are so doing that on purpose.

44
00:03:05,901 --> 00:03:07,110
[Hina] Whoa, rude much!

45
00:03:07,819 --> 00:03:10,864
As if I'm trying to find
an excuse to talk to you.

46
00:03:10,947 --> 00:03:11,823
[gasps softly]

47
00:03:16,202 --> 00:03:17,162
[gasps softly]

48
00:03:19,706 --> 00:03:22,375
Hina, could you and I go talk for a sec?

49
00:03:23,752 --> 00:03:24,586
Hm?

50
00:03:25,962 --> 00:03:27,130
So what's up?

51
00:03:29,507 --> 00:03:31,176
Wait, are you gonna do something weird?

52
00:03:31,259 --> 00:03:33,053
Don't make jokes that are hard to follow!

53
00:03:33,136 --> 00:03:34,763
I was only trying to lighten the mood.

54
00:03:35,889 --> 00:03:36,890
So, Hina,

55
00:03:36,973 --> 00:03:39,768
you said the other day,
that you don't need an answer yet, right?

56
00:03:40,435 --> 00:03:41,478
Yeah.

57
00:03:41,561 --> 00:03:42,520
But the thing is,

58
00:03:43,230 --> 00:03:45,774
I do have feelings for Chinatsu...

59
00:03:46,608 --> 00:03:48,777
so I would like
to give that a shot myself.

60
00:03:49,444 --> 00:03:50,695
Would that be okay?

61
00:03:51,863 --> 00:03:53,531
What? Yeah, for sure.

62
00:03:53,615 --> 00:03:54,824
[gasps softly]

63
00:03:56,117 --> 00:03:57,202
It's like I said,

64
00:03:57,285 --> 00:04:00,038
I know how you feel about her,
so I can understand.

65
00:04:03,124 --> 00:04:05,543
It'd be more annoying
if you held back because of me.

66
00:04:17,013 --> 00:04:18,306
[Kyo] <i>Of course it's not okay.</i>

67
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:20,809
[basketball dribbling]

68
00:04:20,892 --> 00:04:23,561
- [girl] Chinatsu!
- [panting]

69
00:04:25,689 --> 00:04:27,065
What are you doing?

70
00:04:27,148 --> 00:04:28,692
Defense is closing you in!

71
00:04:29,276 --> 00:04:30,568
You've got the other side too!

72
00:04:30,652 --> 00:04:31,820
Got it!

73
00:04:33,405 --> 00:04:36,825
- He is really tough on Chii, huh?
- That's how it has to be.

74
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:39,369
All the upperclassmen are gone now.

75
00:04:39,911 --> 00:04:41,579
It is hard on her, yeah,

76
00:04:41,663 --> 00:04:45,875
but he wants her to be a player
who can make that winning shot.

77
00:04:51,923 --> 00:04:53,842
[inaudible]

78
00:05:00,015 --> 00:05:01,224
[girl] What did the coach say?

79
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:03,768
[Chinatsu] That, since Yoshitani retired,

80
00:05:03,852 --> 00:05:06,563
I should keep up the hard work
and step up as vice-captain.

81
00:05:06,646 --> 00:05:07,480
Yo, I knew it!

82
00:05:07,564 --> 00:05:10,066
[girl] Our next captain's
gonna be Chinatsu!

83
00:05:10,150 --> 00:05:11,776
[Tagawa] You've got the skills to do it,

84
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:14,237
and the younger players
really look up to you.

85
00:05:15,155 --> 00:05:17,240
[Nagisa] Do you actually want to though?

86
00:05:18,158 --> 00:05:19,993
Isn't leading not really your thing?

87
00:05:20,076 --> 00:05:22,454
I was our class representative for a term!

88
00:05:22,537 --> 00:05:24,372
'Cause you lost rock-paper-scissors.

89
00:05:25,498 --> 00:05:27,751
I do feel like the pressure's on...

90
00:05:27,834 --> 00:05:30,503
but I'd do anything for this team.

91
00:05:30,587 --> 00:05:33,423
- Well said, well said!
- I'm behind you, Vice-Captain!

92
00:05:33,506 --> 00:05:34,507
Very cool!

93
00:05:34,591 --> 00:05:37,510
- [girls chattering indistinctly]
- [Chinatsu chuckling]

94
00:05:40,597 --> 00:05:42,265
[basketball dribbling]

95
00:05:59,783 --> 00:06:00,992
[teacher] Excuse me!

96
00:06:01,576 --> 00:06:02,994
It's time for me to lock up!

97
00:06:03,078 --> 00:06:04,245
Understood!

98
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:14,130
[phone vibrates]

99
00:06:18,968 --> 00:06:20,136
MOM

100
00:06:21,888 --> 00:06:22,889
Hello? Mom?

101
00:06:22,972 --> 00:06:25,892
<i>Chinatsu! Happy birthday!</i>

102
00:06:26,684 --> 00:06:29,521
<i>Whoa, Mom, my ears
are ringing after that one.</i>

103
00:06:29,604 --> 00:06:32,899
My voice had to make it all the way
to Japan, can you blame me?

104
00:06:33,858 --> 00:06:35,985
<i>So, any news to report?</i>

105
00:06:36,653 --> 00:06:37,904
Nothing really.

106
00:06:38,488 --> 00:06:42,325
<i>Are you sure?
You don't sound completely like yourself.</i>

107
00:06:42,408 --> 00:06:45,703
The phone can do that
to your voice sometimes, but I'm okay.

108
00:06:45,787 --> 00:06:47,413
<i>Oh, that's what it is.</i>

109
00:06:50,917 --> 00:06:52,961
<i>It's not that I have news...</i>

110
00:06:53,044 --> 00:06:54,045
Hm?

111
00:06:54,796 --> 00:06:57,132
...but I got chosen as vice-captain.

112
00:06:57,215 --> 00:06:58,925
<i>That's amazing!</i>

113
00:06:59,592 --> 00:07:02,178
Coach and Kikuchi
really wanted me to take the role,

114
00:07:02,262 --> 00:07:04,681
so I wanna give it my all, but...

115
00:07:05,515 --> 00:07:07,725
<i>I think I told you last time we talked...</i>

116
00:07:07,809 --> 00:07:11,312
<i>I missed a shot at nationals
when it really mattered.</i>

117
00:07:12,105 --> 00:07:14,315
Even though I had practiced
the best I could,

118
00:07:15,275 --> 00:07:16,818
I still missed it.

119
00:07:19,154 --> 00:07:20,238
[moody music playing]

120
00:07:20,321 --> 00:07:24,659
Honestly, I still have so much work to do
to improve myself as a player.

121
00:07:24,742 --> 00:07:27,579
I don't know how I can focus
on the rest of team too.

122
00:07:28,872 --> 00:07:31,332
I think I'm not ready for this, you know?

123
00:07:33,334 --> 00:07:35,587
[sighs] Listen, Chinatsu.

124
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:38,590
<i>It's not too late to think about that
after you've tried.</i>

125
00:07:38,673 --> 00:07:41,342
<i>It's okay to give this a shot
and have it not go well.</i>

126
00:07:42,427 --> 00:07:43,887
<i>If and when that happens,</i>

127
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:46,473
<i>rather than thinking
it didn't work because of you,</i>

128
00:07:46,556 --> 00:07:49,726
<i>think about everything you learned
from the experience.</i>

129
00:07:50,518 --> 00:07:54,189
If there's anything you should be
keeping in mind going forward,

130
00:07:54,272 --> 00:07:57,984
it's who you're going to rely on
when you're thinking that way.

131
00:07:58,067 --> 00:07:59,486
[exclaims softly]

132
00:07:59,569 --> 00:08:03,740
Being relied on by other people
can be a pretty nice feeling, you know.

133
00:08:04,574 --> 00:08:06,743
<i>All right. I should be going.</i>

134
00:08:06,826 --> 00:08:08,286
Yeah. Thanks.

135
00:08:13,833 --> 00:08:15,752
{\an8}MOM - NAGISA
YUKIKO INOMATA - KIKUCHI SENPAI

136
00:08:16,753 --> 00:08:18,004
[sighs]

137
00:08:20,882 --> 00:08:21,758
HEY, HEY

138
00:08:21,841 --> 00:08:23,051
- [phone chimes]
- [Taiki grunts]

139
00:08:23,134 --> 00:08:24,135
[Chinatsu gasps softly]

140
00:08:24,761 --> 00:08:25,637
Huh?

141
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:26,804
[grunts nervously]

142
00:08:27,597 --> 00:08:30,058
Wait! I swear I wasn't stalking you!

143
00:08:32,018 --> 00:08:33,311
It's a coincidence.

144
00:08:34,854 --> 00:08:37,023
<i>But hang on... this sticker...</i>

145
00:08:38,316 --> 00:08:40,568
<i>I didn't think she'd send me this again.</i>

146
00:08:48,910 --> 00:08:50,286
I wanna go somewhere.

147
00:08:53,706 --> 00:08:55,959
[Taiki] Do you mind a train ride?

148
00:09:05,176 --> 00:09:06,928
Just a bit longer, I promise.

149
00:09:07,762 --> 00:09:08,805
Okay.

150
00:09:15,645 --> 00:09:16,771
[gasps]

151
00:09:17,689 --> 00:09:19,190
[uplifting music playing]

152
00:09:22,485 --> 00:09:24,028
[exclaims]

153
00:09:25,822 --> 00:09:27,073
[Chinatsu] The ocean!

154
00:09:29,075 --> 00:09:32,370
Back in grade school,
I used to come here pretty often.

155
00:09:32,453 --> 00:09:34,872
The sun's about to set,
so you can't swim, but...

156
00:09:36,791 --> 00:09:38,876
[giggles]

157
00:09:43,047 --> 00:09:45,383
[Taiki] <i>There's that
childlike side of her.</i>

158
00:09:46,217 --> 00:09:48,219
[Chinatsu giggling]

159
00:09:52,473 --> 00:09:53,766
[gasps softly]

160
00:09:56,644 --> 00:09:57,645
[Taiki] <i>I'm glad.</i>

161
00:09:58,646 --> 00:10:00,523
<i>Seems like this cheered her up a bit.</i>

162
00:10:00,607 --> 00:10:02,900
Come on, Taiki, you gotta join me in here!

163
00:10:03,526 --> 00:10:04,652
[Taiki] Just a second!

164
00:10:10,992 --> 00:10:12,493
[Chinatsu] Hurry up, hurry up!

165
00:10:13,244 --> 00:10:17,165
[exclaims] Chinatsu, your wish bracelet...

166
00:10:17,248 --> 00:10:20,418
Yeah. I don't have it. It finally broke.

167
00:10:22,003 --> 00:10:24,505
I guess we piled on
too many wishes after all.

168
00:10:25,006 --> 00:10:26,424
That's too bad.

169
00:10:31,054 --> 00:10:32,347
[Taiki] <i>That's too bad.</i>

170
00:10:33,222 --> 00:10:35,183
We don't match anymore, do we?

171
00:10:42,398 --> 00:10:43,358
[grunts]

172
00:10:44,776 --> 00:10:46,194
What did you do that for?

173
00:10:46,277 --> 00:10:48,738
You were just standing there,
all spaced out.

174
00:10:48,821 --> 00:10:49,697
And again!

175
00:10:51,032 --> 00:10:52,116
You'll pay for that!

176
00:10:53,451 --> 00:10:55,703
[both chuckle]

177
00:10:56,537 --> 00:10:57,705
[Taiki] Hold on! Wait!

178
00:10:58,665 --> 00:11:00,708
- [Chinatsu] I'm going again!
- Agh! It's so cold!

179
00:11:00,792 --> 00:11:04,629
Looky there. Didn't realize
young couples still did stuff like that.

180
00:11:05,213 --> 00:11:08,216
They're shining as brightly
as the sun behind them.

181
00:11:08,299 --> 00:11:13,137
Although, it looks like the weather's
about to take a turn for the worse.

182
00:11:13,805 --> 00:11:16,974
Chinatsu, time out, hold on.

183
00:11:17,058 --> 00:11:19,519
The sand around this area makes you sink.

184
00:11:19,602 --> 00:11:21,979
- Is that even a thing here?
- I'm telling the truth!

185
00:11:22,605 --> 00:11:24,482
- You gotta be careful.
- [Chinatsu exclaims]

186
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:30,405
[soft piano music playing]

187
00:11:38,121 --> 00:11:40,248
- Thanks.
- [Taiki] No worries.

188
00:11:42,625 --> 00:11:43,543
Huh?

189
00:11:45,044 --> 00:11:48,005
I don't think
we want you falling in, right?

190
00:11:48,089 --> 00:11:50,007
Oh... Right.

191
00:11:51,092 --> 00:11:53,052
[grunts, yells in agony]

192
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:06,732
[Chinatsu] It's a good thing
you had your sweatpants with you.

193
00:12:06,816 --> 00:12:08,276
[Taiki groans]

194
00:12:08,359 --> 00:12:10,278
[Taiki] <i>This outfit looks ridiculous!</i>

195
00:12:10,361 --> 00:12:12,655
Am I really riding the train like this?

196
00:12:12,738 --> 00:12:14,949
Your other pants won't be dry in time.

197
00:12:17,285 --> 00:12:19,787
Let's head back after the sun sets.

198
00:12:23,749 --> 00:12:26,294
Thanks for bringing me, Taiki. It's great.

199
00:12:29,630 --> 00:12:31,132
Chinatsu...

200
00:12:31,215 --> 00:12:33,301
today is your birthday, right?

201
00:12:33,384 --> 00:12:34,302
[Chinatsu] Mm-hm.

202
00:12:34,385 --> 00:12:37,054
I actually have a present for you.

203
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,390
It's a small thing, but...

204
00:12:43,561 --> 00:12:44,687
Cake?

205
00:12:45,313 --> 00:12:47,231
You had this the whole time?

206
00:12:47,315 --> 00:12:50,151
I asked them to give me
a lot of ice packs for it.

207
00:12:50,943 --> 00:12:52,862
And I, of course, brought the candles.

208
00:12:53,738 --> 00:12:56,574
I can't believe I'm 17 already.

209
00:12:58,201 --> 00:13:00,578
Birthdays really do matter, huh?

210
00:13:00,661 --> 00:13:03,289
You feel yourself
inching toward becoming an adult.

211
00:13:04,415 --> 00:13:06,459
Your birthday is in January, right?

212
00:13:06,542 --> 00:13:08,753
Yeah. It's on January 15th.

213
00:13:09,837 --> 00:13:14,467
[Chinatsu] So, since you're 15 right now,
we're two years apart.

214
00:13:14,550 --> 00:13:17,595
Being two years apart,
it isn't that big a deal.

215
00:13:18,763 --> 00:13:19,889
You're right.

216
00:13:24,685 --> 00:13:27,104
Until we're adults, we're still kids!

217
00:13:27,188 --> 00:13:29,690
All right, and now for the singing!

218
00:13:30,483 --> 00:13:33,903
<i>- ♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>
- You're singing?

219
00:13:33,986 --> 00:13:37,823
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

220
00:13:37,907 --> 00:13:41,285
<i>♪ Happy birthday, dear... ♪</i>

221
00:13:41,369 --> 00:13:43,788
<i>♪ Chinatsu ♪</i>

222
00:13:45,331 --> 00:13:49,418
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

223
00:13:49,502 --> 00:13:50,878
[wind blowing]

224
00:13:52,880 --> 00:13:54,924
Oh, the wind did it for me.

225
00:13:55,007 --> 00:13:56,175
Should I relight them?

226
00:13:56,259 --> 00:13:57,343
It's okay.

227
00:14:01,556 --> 00:14:02,557
Let's eat.

228
00:14:13,317 --> 00:14:15,736
- You know what? About the wish bracelet...
- Mm?

229
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:18,364
We'll be matching again
before you know it.

230
00:14:20,950 --> 00:14:23,578
'Cause next year, mine's gonna come off.

231
00:14:24,328 --> 00:14:26,414
Uh. [chuckles]

232
00:14:27,164 --> 00:14:28,916
[Taiki] What are you laughing at?

233
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,418
[Chinatsu] Mm... It's nothing.

234
00:14:30,501 --> 00:14:32,628
[Taiki] Ugh, why do I feel like
there is something?

235
00:14:32,712 --> 00:14:37,091
[Chinatsu] It's just, I was thinking
how you can be randomly cheesy sometimes.

236
00:14:37,174 --> 00:14:38,175
[Taiki] What?

237
00:14:41,178 --> 00:14:42,597
[Taiki] C'mon, this way!

238
00:14:48,936 --> 00:14:50,730
The rain came outta nowhere.

239
00:14:50,813 --> 00:14:52,607
I got wet after all.

240
00:14:53,482 --> 00:14:55,610
Mom's gonna give me an earful when we--

241
00:14:55,693 --> 00:14:57,612
{\an8}OUT OF SERVICE
DUE TO LANDSLIDE

242
00:14:58,404 --> 00:14:59,614
{\an8}[both] Huh?

243
00:14:59,697 --> 00:15:01,616
{\an8}OUT OF SERVICE

244
00:15:02,283 --> 00:15:03,743
[Taiki groans]

245
00:15:03,826 --> 00:15:04,869
[both] What?

246
00:15:08,706 --> 00:15:12,126
GUESTHOUSE SIOMIHAMA

247
00:15:12,209 --> 00:15:14,879
[Taiki] Yeah. I know, I'm sorry.

248
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:18,549
We were at the beach,
and there was a landslide.

249
00:15:18,633 --> 00:15:21,385
Yeah. They only had one room open.

250
00:15:22,511 --> 00:15:24,388
It's fine, my friends are here too.

251
00:15:25,014 --> 00:15:27,058
Yeah. Sure thing.

252
00:15:27,141 --> 00:15:28,267
Talk soon.

253
00:15:30,436 --> 00:15:31,437
[sighs]

254
00:15:32,229 --> 00:15:34,649
<i>No, nothing about this is fine!</i>

255
00:15:35,274 --> 00:15:37,360
<i>There's a landslide, so we can't go home,</i>

256
00:15:37,443 --> 00:15:39,654
<i>there's only one room
at the inn we ran into,</i>

257
00:15:39,737 --> 00:15:42,198
<i>I lied to my mom that my friends
are here with us...</i>

258
00:15:43,991 --> 00:15:47,328
<i>and I'm staying in the same room
with Chinatsu all night!</i>

259
00:15:49,121 --> 00:15:51,666
<i>I mean, I'm not gonna do anything weird.</i>

260
00:15:51,749 --> 00:15:55,920
<i>Really, I'm more worried that she might be
disappointed that her birthday,</i>

261
00:15:56,003 --> 00:15:58,130
<i>of all days, turned out like this.</i>

262
00:16:01,509 --> 00:16:03,678
Are you done on the phone?

263
00:16:03,761 --> 00:16:05,054
[gasps softly]

264
00:16:06,138 --> 00:16:07,473
What did Yukiko say?

265
00:16:08,099 --> 00:16:10,059
Huh? Uh...

266
00:16:10,601 --> 00:16:12,645
Well, she told us to be careful.

267
00:16:13,354 --> 00:16:14,438
Ah.

268
00:16:15,022 --> 00:16:16,440
[Taiki] <i>Oh, man, I'm doomed!</i>

269
00:16:17,066 --> 00:16:19,735
<i>There's no way
I'm getting any sleep tonight.</i>

270
00:16:19,819 --> 00:16:21,195
- Taiki.
- [grunts]

271
00:16:21,278 --> 00:16:23,698
{\an8}GAME OF LIVES

272
00:16:23,781 --> 00:16:26,075
They had all of these in the lobby!

273
00:16:26,158 --> 00:16:27,201
Let's play together!

274
00:16:27,785 --> 00:16:29,704
Since we have to stay overnight,

275
00:16:29,787 --> 00:16:31,706
we might as well
do a board game all-nighter!

276
00:16:33,082 --> 00:16:34,667
What should we play?

277
00:16:37,003 --> 00:16:39,588
I'm really good with whatever.
It's your birthday.

278
00:16:39,672 --> 00:16:42,008
You're right. Today is my birthday.

279
00:16:45,511 --> 00:16:46,595
[Taiki] <i>She's fast.</i>

280
00:16:47,221 --> 00:16:49,223
- I can be the dealer.
- [phone vibrates]

281
00:16:49,932 --> 00:16:50,975
NAGISA

282
00:16:51,058 --> 00:16:52,601
[Chinatsu] Oh. Nagisa's calling me.

283
00:16:53,310 --> 00:16:55,104
Sorry, do you mind?

284
00:16:55,187 --> 00:16:57,606
No. Should I give you some space, then?

285
00:16:57,690 --> 00:16:59,108
That's okay.

286
00:16:59,191 --> 00:17:00,359
<i>Oh.</i>

287
00:17:00,443 --> 00:17:02,278
[Chinatsu] Oh, it's a video call.

288
00:17:02,361 --> 00:17:03,362
Huh?

289
00:17:03,446 --> 00:17:05,489
<i>A very happy birthday!</i>

290
00:17:05,573 --> 00:17:06,824
<i>This is part two!</i>

291
00:17:07,992 --> 00:17:08,993
Thanks, Nagisa!

292
00:17:10,703 --> 00:17:13,414
[Taiki] <i>Wait. Did I need to hide?</i>

293
00:17:13,497 --> 00:17:16,167
Were you just calling
to celebrate with me again?

294
00:17:16,250 --> 00:17:19,628
<i>And there's also something
that I've been wanting to tell you.</i>

295
00:17:20,963 --> 00:17:23,549
Today or, more like recently,

296
00:17:23,632 --> 00:17:26,135
it seems like you've been down
and not feeling yourself.

297
00:17:26,927 --> 00:17:27,887
[Chinatsu sighs]

298
00:17:28,512 --> 00:17:29,972
<i>I know you're under pressure,</i>

299
00:17:30,056 --> 00:17:33,017
<i>but I've got your back
and I'm here for you.</i>

300
00:17:33,100 --> 00:17:34,560
<i>We'll keep getting better.</i>

301
00:17:34,643 --> 00:17:35,895
<i>I know that we will.</i>

302
00:17:36,979 --> 00:17:38,397
<i>Let's do this as a team.</i>

303
00:17:39,565 --> 00:17:41,442
[Chinatsu] Yeah. Thanks.

304
00:17:43,235 --> 00:17:48,491
<i>So that's what I wanted to say to you,
but you already seem more relaxed.</i>

305
00:17:48,574 --> 00:17:49,408
Huh?

306
00:17:49,492 --> 00:17:52,870
You were kinda giving off
negative vibes at practice earlier.

307
00:17:52,953 --> 00:17:55,414
<i>Well, any bad mood
is bound to pass at some point!</i>

308
00:17:55,498 --> 00:17:56,665
Can't argue with that.

309
00:17:57,666 --> 00:18:00,419
Wait a sec. I just noticed
you're wearing a <i>yukata.</i>

310
00:18:01,212 --> 00:18:02,755
<i>Like you wear at an inn...</i>

311
00:18:02,838 --> 00:18:05,841
[Chinatsu] Yeah. I'm staying
with my extended family.

312
00:18:06,509 --> 00:18:09,386
<i>It all makes sense now,
that's why you're more upbeat.</i>

313
00:18:09,470 --> 00:18:12,098
[chuckles] <i>You were bummed
you couldn't wear a</i> yukata

314
00:18:12,181 --> 00:18:14,058
<i>to the fireworks festival, remember?</i>

315
00:18:14,141 --> 00:18:15,810
That's not true, you're making that up.

316
00:18:16,477 --> 00:18:19,855
<i>Lies. I saw you eyeing
everybody wearing one!</i>

317
00:18:19,939 --> 00:18:21,941
[Chinatsu] You were, too, Nagisa.

318
00:18:22,024 --> 00:18:25,736
[Taiki] <i>I will say, I'm glad I got to see
Chinatsu wearing a</i> yukata.

319
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:28,239
<i>- All right, I'm gonna get going.</i>
- See ya.

320
00:18:30,324 --> 00:18:31,826
[grunts]

321
00:18:32,910 --> 00:18:33,828
[exclaims]

322
00:18:33,911 --> 00:18:34,829
NAGISA
CALL ENDED

323
00:18:36,664 --> 00:18:37,706
Whoa, nice catch.

324
00:18:37,790 --> 00:18:39,250
But she heard me yell.

325
00:18:39,333 --> 00:18:42,086
Don't worry about it.
She had hung up the phone already.

326
00:18:45,339 --> 00:18:47,591
<i>Was that a man's voice just now?</i>

327
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:49,593
<i>Maybe her uncle?</i>

328
00:18:50,469 --> 00:18:52,138
Okay then, that's a relief.

329
00:18:53,222 --> 00:18:56,100
- Nagisa really is a good friend.
- Isn't she?

330
00:18:56,183 --> 00:18:59,728
All the people in my life are kind.
I'm lucky.

331
00:19:03,315 --> 00:19:04,400
Actually,

332
00:19:05,025 --> 00:19:09,071
I wanted to apologize
about the fireworks festival.

333
00:19:09,572 --> 00:19:10,489
Huh?

334
00:19:10,573 --> 00:19:12,908
When we talked about it at home,

335
00:19:12,992 --> 00:19:15,995
I think I said
I was going with my friends.

336
00:19:16,078 --> 00:19:18,873
But no one else we asked
was able to join us,

337
00:19:18,956 --> 00:19:21,167
and then Kyo got a fever the day of...

338
00:19:22,126 --> 00:19:23,544
so I didn't go in a group.

339
00:19:24,962 --> 00:19:27,506
And it ended up looking
like I'd lied about it.

340
00:19:27,590 --> 00:19:29,508
- [gasps softly]
- So I...

341
00:19:30,342 --> 00:19:31,260
am sorry.

342
00:19:35,347 --> 00:19:38,809
You don't have to make a big deal
about something like that, Taiki.

343
00:19:38,893 --> 00:19:41,145
Well, okay, you might be right, but...

344
00:19:42,146 --> 00:19:45,524
even so, I still wanted
to apologize for it.

345
00:19:45,608 --> 00:19:46,984
[chuckles softly]

346
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:51,989
Okay then, I also have something
I want to apologize for.

347
00:19:52,072 --> 00:19:53,532
Wait, what is it?

348
00:19:54,158 --> 00:19:56,285
I want to take back what I said to you.

349
00:19:56,994 --> 00:19:58,787
About it not being a good thing.

350
00:19:58,871 --> 00:19:59,997
[gasps softly]

351
00:20:00,623 --> 00:20:02,541
<i>I drew a boundary between us,</i>

352
00:20:02,625 --> 00:20:05,544
<i>and probably made you feel like
you had to keep your distance.</i>

353
00:20:06,503 --> 00:20:09,298
I think it was a bit harsh of me
to do that to you.

354
00:20:09,381 --> 00:20:11,050
No, no, it wasn't...

355
00:20:12,176 --> 00:20:14,595
[Taiki] <i>I do understand
where she's coming from.</i>

356
00:20:15,346 --> 00:20:16,472
And so...

357
00:20:17,097 --> 00:20:18,307
[sighs]

358
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:22,311
I hope that you can accept my apology.

359
00:20:22,394 --> 00:20:24,772
You don't have to make
a big deal about it.

360
00:20:24,855 --> 00:20:25,856
Huh?

361
00:20:28,984 --> 00:20:31,070
I think we can call it even.

362
00:20:33,155 --> 00:20:34,573
[chuckles softly]

363
00:20:34,657 --> 00:20:36,825
All right, now let's play a game.

364
00:20:37,409 --> 00:20:39,328
With two players, how 'bout Last Card?

365
00:20:39,411 --> 00:20:41,789
- Oh, I haven't played that.
- Really?

366
00:20:43,916 --> 00:20:45,334
[birds chirping]

367
00:20:53,175 --> 00:20:54,551
[groans softly]

368
00:21:09,191 --> 00:21:12,069
[snoring softly]

369
00:21:13,946 --> 00:21:16,824
<i>Why didn't he just sleep on the futon?</i>

370
00:21:16,907 --> 00:21:18,617
<i>He's gonna be all sore.</i>

371
00:21:18,701 --> 00:21:20,077
[pleasant music playing]

372
00:21:35,718 --> 00:21:36,760
Hm?

373
00:21:40,723 --> 00:21:42,141
Hmm?

374
00:21:43,225 --> 00:21:44,351
[grunts]

375
00:21:47,187 --> 00:21:48,856
[chuckles]

376
00:21:59,199 --> 00:22:00,409
[Chinatsu] <i>Good morning...</i>

377
00:22:02,453 --> 00:22:03,912
<i>17-year-old me.</i>

378
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
